plurx-player (0.1.1+lp7.360.1.mpv0.41.0-1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Launcher (milestone M4): redeem, decide, play in mpv, heartbeat,
    progress, seek re-creation, teardown.
  * Package a private libplacebo 7.360.1 and mpv 0.41.0, the versions
    Ubuntu 26.10 ships, under /usr/lib/plurx-player (milestone M5
    packaging). mpv is linked with DT_RPATH $ORIGIN/../lib and leaves no
    build path behind.
  * Build from a Debian source package (3.0 (quilt)): the launcher is the
    main orig tarball and the pinned libplacebo and mpv tarballs are its
    component orig tarballs, so the corresponding source of the GPL mpv and
    LGPL libplacebo binaries is published beside the .deb.
  * Apply the patch series from packaging/patches/<name>/series, exactly.
    It is empty until the Dolby Vision closed-form patches land.
  * Run mpv with plurx Player's own --config-dir
    ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/plurx-player/mpv), never the general ~/.config/mpv,
    with --ytdl=no, and without LD_LIBRARY_PATH, LD_PRELOAD or LD_AUDIT.
  * Byte-compile the launcher with dh_python3, whose prerm removes every
    .pyc, so removal leaves nothing behind.
  * Add the plurx-player(1) manual page. Recommend desktop-file-utils and a
    Vulkan driver; record the statically linked glslang and SPIRV-Tools in
    Built-Using and debian/copyright.

 -- plurx maintainers <noreply@plurx.invalid>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
